  "reasons": {
    "extensions / archive": "Archive format and filter error paths include third-party-library and malformed-input alternatives that are not all reachable in one GCC/Linux coverage run.",
    "extensions / FUSE": "FUSE's dynamic-loader alternatives, fatal-signal handler, mount-failure variants, and spontaneous-session-exit path are mutually exclusive or process-disrupting in one GCC/Linux coverage run. Public filesystem behavior and deterministic lifecycle failures remain covered.",
    "extensions / language database": "The new embedded-database module's remaining branches are compiler-expanded fatal-invariant paths around the generated, build-time-verified payload. Brotli success, corrupt input, and decoded-size mismatch are covered directly; the high target remains the graduation boundary."
  },
